[ system ]
You are reading how a guard's questioning of a wanted companion ended, from the conversation alone. Time is up and neither side took a step, so decide what the conversation itself settled. Output ONLY a JSON object.

## The Charge

{{ guard }}, a guard, stopped {{ suspect }}, a companion of {{ player }}, over a {{ bounty }} gold bounty in {{ hold }}{% if charges and charges != "" %} for {{ charges }}{% endif %}.
{% if bribe %}
The bounty was too large for a plain fine: the guard would take a bribe of {{ cost }} gold.
{% else %}
The fine was {{ cost }} gold.
{% endif %}

## What Was Said

{% set transcript = default(transcript, []) %}
{% if length(transcript) > 0 %}
{% for line in transcript %}
- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
(No conversation was captured.)
{% endif %}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
Decide how the conversation ended.

- "waived" - {{ guard }} was convinced, took pity or let it go: {{ suspect }} walks free and the charge is dropped.
- "paid" - {{ suspect }} agreed to pay the fine or the bribe and {{ guard }} accepted it.
- "custody" - {{ guard }} insisted on taking {{ suspect }} in, or {{ suspect }} agreed to go. This is the default whenever you are unsure.
- "refused" - {{ suspect }} openly refused to be taken and was ready to fight.

Respond with ONLY one of these JSON objects. No explanation. One line:
{% raw %}{"verdict": "waived"}{% endraw %}
{% raw %}{"verdict": "paid"}{% endraw %}
{% raw %}{"verdict": "custody"}{% endraw %}
{% raw %}{"verdict": "refused"}{% endraw %}
[ end user ]
